The Web Crypto API (`window.crypto.subtle`) provides powerful low-level cryptographic functions[4]. Per the W3C Web Cryptography specification and browser security policies, these features are restricted to **Secure Contexts** to prevent malicious scripts from arbitrarily handling sensitive cryptographic keys or data[2][5]. \n* **Secure contexts** are defined as pages delivered via **HTTPS**, or locally via **`localhost` / `127.0.0.1`**[2][3].\n* The **`file://` protocol** lacks a secure origin concept (mapping to an opaque origin of `null`), meaning browsers disable `crypto.subtle` entirely[3][1].\n\n---\n\n### Browser Behavior Matrix (`file://` protocol)\n\n| Browser | Behavior with `file://` (`crypto.subtle`) | Console Error / Symptom |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Google Chrome / Edge** | `window.crypto.subtle` is **`undefined`**[5][3] | `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'digest' / 'encrypt' / etc.)`[3] |\n| **Mozilla Firefox** | `window.crypto.subtle` is **`undefined`**[3] | `TypeError: window.crypto.subtle is undefined`[3] |\n| **Apple Safari** | `window.crypto.subtle` may be undefined or throw security/secure-context exceptions depending on the OS/Safari version. | Restricted due to lack of secure context. |\n\n---\n\n### How to Fix It\n\nTo use `window.crypto.subtle`, you must stop running your file through the `file://` protocol and instead serve it through a local development web server using `http://localhost`[6][7]. \n\nQuick ways to spin up a local server include:\n\n1. **VS Code (Live Server Extension):**\n   * Install the *Live Server* extension by Ritwick Dey[6][8].\n   * Right-click your HTML file inside VS Code and select **\"Open with Live Server\"**[6]. It will automatically serve your page at `http://127.0.0.1:[port]`[3].\n2. **Node.js (`npx serve`):**\n   * Open your project folder in a terminal and run[6]:\n     ```bash\n     npx serve\n     ```\n   * Open the provided `http://localhost:[port]` URL in your browser[6].\n3. **Python (Built-in Server):**\n   * Run the following command in your project directory:\n     * **Python 3:** `python3 -m http.server`\n     * **Python 2:** `python -m SimpleHTTPServer`\n   * Navigate to `http://localhost:8000` in your browser.\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH0whcEigwKI1qzZ4GwBQyNBKe1c5lxa6E30CpmPRyw_S7tJ7QWjhCYXGTuImZD4YR7z1j_iBUeYwgW13ccTBJ8T62c1uyjbx76pnZDOW2wqRJzrqsi5oeY3X3xdLTX44DhiivVvVt5Vvywjsp4l899VewSr6LKcHY=)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG5z_-BBvuKF28xbrffmiHTVw2WdOJcf5YuZgpE1yZNFxSJIBAAu7WODZ2shjmghQSipG_oO-oAggIypH42GkGkHpDLtEQdIlXLLptLzA9a52E21-rACYplLsdoQHITfgCrn_ecytxHgx1OP764dziOH7b6ihwBMbU6-aW5gcy9PWobHGwYyi7SoNKGJxPj_c7tYdy-JCv0XodBUoKPE1aXCRmAfLPURA_8lereEYF6dg==)\n[3] [authgear.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_jUMFZRX0m39qIx_2WKPwgdZCPPKJc2W81gCIc05Mrlwy4Mk9OCqErZgiQqA6PZshmqZOCgU-Lg-NncaW_PhZV9fI9u9r3GASrriE8YjNSjtL-zkMCg7pURDxnpGA7p20vSSd0JaarDVRajoXz8y5j6hptcnGdRZDCxFR9xkyzqtSLr7VDOjk2kccbCrEAQjApi1_by2gIWu-wBftrg==)\n[4] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjGHrYSobaTc77cEqOHGYtCwSVpIQ_MxelnSref1hv8ldR84WLm4lB5XdKZLvaQ-6HNsZTzxZz6FpjqkNOUUtXEPWbuVnjGT02g40uk4LdpqY9OX2BFTzUT-5NUiEtn4BjWEeJZTGINn5Eflae5Io1EbQZ)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHrZ5q8_q7ODAfhrSifhYctNjsthTfM5GLpjYSgol66fDyyz3bTgrv2IxqotSjpZNpTZRer9VFF-jYOnghizMT8h1F6aF4k9F9UOuAkQJEgCkp6h7Zt2zNyITCNitDPKR8NBcw_KvihNkpX-XQstEwtb4mm1fRI-Qz8K1SYZTkoR2FFWsXwGI45KTUP9jOFo3ERmWLXVUEUr5snYmpmdJeI1w9Dd13)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrK0MU32IiXgqKaItVmjq38yihJi_S2fCFebMOzI-U7w2Ko2M74vQbGV2AKKNdM5fDv3G5aRNsxOaiefhdcbKvTxJcNhD-bbuiGELzDFTzJ9A3mV-JQeOEqpEz8BMEM-wb-uB3VHASp81hsMmO-cjl6xFLxGxoKtODZTnVxL9fkO9p9FoJiDfHXU7yqchAsuCb