{"step_index":856,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:24Z","input_tokens":3771,"cache_read_tokens":278355,"output_tokens":197,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: Firestore document structure is key. Need to understand `fields` with its types (`stringValue`, etc.), especially for `PATCH` operations (`updateMask`), and creation (`POST`). Also need to know how to retrieve docs (`GET`).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"firestore rest api documents batchWrite commit delete json format v1"}},{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"firestore rest api value types mapValue arrayValue integerValue stringValue booleanValue"}}]}
{"step_index":857,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:34+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:34+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore rest api documents batchWrite commit delete json format v1\" returned the following summary:\nIn the Google Cloud Firestore REST API (v1), there are two distinct ways to execute multiple write and delete operations:\n\n1. **`documents:batchWrite`**: Applies a batch of writes **non-atomically** and independently. Operations can execute out of order, and you cannot have more than one write per document in a single request[1].\n2. **`documents:commit`**: Commits a set of writes **atomically** (either all succeed or all fail together) and in strict order[2].\n\n---\n\n### 1. Endpoint URLs\n\n* **Batch Write (`batchWrite`)**:\n  ```http\n  POST https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{projectId}/databases/{databaseId}/documents:batchWrite\n  ```\n* **Atomic Commit (`commit`)**:\n  ```http\n  POST https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{projectId}/databases/{databaseId}/documents:commit\n  ```\n  *(Note: For default databases, `{databaseId}` is usually `(default)`[3]).*\n\n---\n\n### 2. JSON Payload Format (`v1`)\n\nBoth endpoints accept a JSON body containing a `writes` array[1][2]. Each element in the array is a `Write` object that can perform operations like `update` (set/upsert), `delete`, or `transform`.\n\n#### Example JSON Payload (Containing a `delete` and an `update`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"writes\": [\n    {\n      \"delete\": \"projects/my-project-id/databases/(default)/documents/users/user_to_delete\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"update\": {\n        \"name\": \"projects/my-project-id/databases/(default)/documents/users/user_to_update\",\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"status\": {\n            \"stringValue\": \"active\"\n          },\n          \"loginCount\": {\n            \"integerValue\": \"5\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"updateMask\": {\n        \"fieldPaths\": [\"status\", \"loginCount\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Detailed Breakdown of Write Operations inside the JSON\n\nInside the `writes` array, you can define different actions per object:\n\n* **Delete a Document:**\n  Provide the fully qualified resource name of the document to the `delete` field[4].\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"delete\": \"projects/{projectId}/databases/{databaseId}/documents/{collection}/{documentId}\"\n  }\n  ```\n\n* **Create / Update (Set) a Document (`update`):**\n  Provide the document path under `name`, wrap your data inside typed `fields`[5], and optionally specify an `updateMask` if you want a partial update (merge behavior)[6].\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"update\": {\n      \"name\": \"projects/{projectId}/databases/{databaseId}/documents/{collection}/{documentId}\",\n      \"fields\": {\n        \"fieldName\": { \"stringValue\": \"text value\" },\n        \"numberField\": { \"integerValue\": \"10\" },\n        \"boolField\": { \"booleanValue\": true }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 4. cURL Example (`commit` endpoint)\n\nHere is a full example using `cURL` to perform an atomic commit containing a document update and a document deletion simultaneously:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \\\n  \"https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/my-project-id/databases/(default)/documents:commit\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OAUTH2_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"writes\": [\n      {\n        \"update\": {\n          \"name\": \"projects/my-project-id/databases/(default)/documents/products/item123\",\n          \"fields\": {\n            \"price\": { \"doubleValue\": 49.99 },\n            \"inStock\": { \"booleanValue\": true }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"delete\": \"projects/my-project-id/databases/(default)/documents/temp-cart/cart999\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }'\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHsTGlMt9PGJdvn8hzrYhncoB7Ojpa6h1cVp038fmdShVMHXOvM7C5NeyCS3hOB0yr3IW0Op_yPl91IuV3c0nMUL7pmWg46tsmTuGUuuEuKt9gflS1SgbOgvBLbufOB03gZUApPfQl07ZYmXHuY7uguJt-uFQXuwKWts3d2QNrxCt9Q6_QUKcFn-BcOK_0qW2Yt2U41avHl9wSp)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0YwawDr6iC1W0F2BalqW8_Q2a9g2UhBT22vaZNu1oja7h1gRMj4qw2WabWr96ojQyzRHXUdEo1w5dn2noMnZtCvLMtJ5TJ-pau8ggv6wEemNb25ocjguW5KlydIuUnKeb79bNSL5bs292YlhsLW5o67dgnnZHo_6QdNz9xo3QDGjDDpgLpy7hijFexT5FdqAQ1xGRFw==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH3j6qXj-X_Pxvt26Q5NGL02w4RsSqb7vOkrnyWQcBXT7fzrWEUoT7s739YwF3IZ7W0cf6O7eoCDHYOa5PbKd4h-Fv3RntmYJCp3-wK6Dqnir1RVLeEmanZynddGlwnpL7-X8vO95IZSopeiWjUP6fxtgVkLYMv2C25)\n[4] [postman.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFm3SDLdBCM-bdxGGzvYJ0mfKIBE8CKLzAV7sB-YuXGnVZExno3eESXAFysbgNb4PV6ZHlpzsiynZbzzDhSUXJntKWBO-xsbjck2GfmPCQSN_7oEa2Xeru60eF5U3cbviGd7wI4r_w5adWFaFm6etXE-GNw9fTRM1zLwsmBiLHyrAynUpToqqUTTJ91KX5MBiMEFL2r8N-7CXMC9YGoQQYIGmD-Nai7)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFLhGUg92MFKD4_tabEE_FGkTqjRqz5_rGka7lKbgmyCeCw0waR3De7wvyhZGxx1_an1cHX4xiCewuSahyWDZ3su6bDTJzuVqjW1t137voXDEX126DW6Tqapd8ylGerYQbA9Vocnu3sx3hmSS4pp6HEEg==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFi_ntAYGK5w1I9jpGr9nFF4ICUT7RuW6O8CyfPmagfAEVUPSRswkIJ-BWUUFVb_YVAPloas3EjhpNRC1DHCThp2-kSrV7gplvswPRNjbjRuwT5fVt-PZmwUVAXDCI4m9dnQKgz6FYO-jbNwDlEebYhVf0Tt2DXa05JskJtuH0xCsSSX4vQpYBUdaFJ0bLruy3q5nQ=)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":858,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:38+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:38+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore rest api value types mapValue arrayValue integerValue stringValue booleanValue\" returned the following summary:\nIn the **Cloud Firestore REST API**, every document field value is wrapped in a type-safe object called a **`Value`**[1]. Because the REST API uses explicit typing instead of standard JSON type inference, you must specify the exact data type wrapper for every field (e.g., `stringValue`, `integerValue`, `booleanValue`, `mapValue`, `arrayValue`)[2][3].\n\nBelow is an overview and JSON payload example demonstrating how to use these specific value types in Firestore REST API requests (`POST` or `PATCH`)[4][3].\n\n---\n\n### 1. `stringValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a UTF-8 text string[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"stringValue\": \"your_string_here\"`[3]\n\n### 2. `integerValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a 64-bit integer (`int64`)[1]. \n* **Important:** In the REST API, integer values must be passed as **strings** (e.g., `\"123\"`) to prevent precision loss in languages/environments that handle JSON numbers as standard floating-point types[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"integerValue\": \"42\"` (or sometimes accepted as a raw number depending on the client library, but strictly specified as a string `string (int64 format)` in the official protocol reference)[1].\n\n### 3. `booleanValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a boolean (`true` or `false`)[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"booleanValue\": true`\n\n### 4. `mapValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a nested object or map containing its own set of fields[5]. It wraps a nested `fields` object[5][4].\n* **JSON Syntax:** \n  ```json\n  \"mapValue\": {\n    \"fields\": {\n      \"nestedFieldKey\": { \"stringValue\": \"nested value\" }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n### 5. `arrayValue`\n* **Description:** Represents an ordered list/array of Firestore `Value` items[1]. It wraps an array called `values`[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** \n  ```json\n  \"arrayValue\": {\n    \"values\": [\n      { \"stringValue\": \"item1\" },\n      { \"integerValue\": \"10\" }\n    ]\n  }\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### Complete Example Payload\n\nHere is how you combine all of these types together into a standard Firestore REST API document body (e.g., when creating or updating a document)[3]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"username\": {\n      \"stringValue\": \"johndoe\"\n    },\n    \"age\": {\n      \"integerValue\": \"30\"\n    },\n    \"isActive\": {\n      \"booleanValue\": true\n    },\n    \"tags\": {\n      \"arrayValue\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          { \"stringValue\": \"admin\" },\n          { \"stringValue\": \"developer\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"address\": {\n      \"mapValue\": {\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"city\": { \"stringValue\": \"New York\" },\n          \"zipCode\": { \"integerValue\": \"10001\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEi6k3_qmcqE1FW5iTFih1Irf9BtgkVsUQzwvOTqwwmDyrsyOmS8blw0eErId-gtTWXOpDwDK5pjU2-9j6b-uZYMQkqOOP4eUizI4hWOzLUcCwaZTVjzfufaE5_Paf-TiNspVBaN2xxraTWkWJLz1O_GHUb3RZWz1D6vSNc4uLiigOGELRC3Q==)\n[2] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHuSuv6OQmixFLSgZM2Nm9filGGWZw-aMADpBVe42oBmVnAeeDN6TNNd8qfCOUCbQRRnn3iOjFMQYAQDJS-BJnurSSYDznL1bZPiHyZA8LxKPALsL5WDBiQnos041d4utxb28DB199CxHtc6hY=)\n[3] [nullisnotanobject.co.uk](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF05LdfqZQ7Rvo5zH7_tiULb3D1GxAaWXkS77QXFHhJyCOkHKJLHRSbDwL--Dt7fR1zkJLQA6moTTjndNU2hvCA5xdq6wCD2vN6mAYpBNCCPPMdJ2DPY9Bn8kdU01N2ofT_mvo2vGvKuZ421Ml4A55eyfZuXXomyQ==)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHy7H35yfroooSq69Hz6ZsyOocAT9M9QymIdqRTnATn4bZQBTeeTzGDGganLv4YVOrh8LeOs1dGbvZJN_3e8CkQsXuOEW6i0SSBB5IZJ5ioZz7wTDGGz9Xxf-7yw5C9Twgft700FrXobIo53iCHofjXnBp0Xq5z1OF2ViqvlUIrUkusUQ==)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEGMv6idIjf6AldX0EybeqmNew3JTBto5qm3srxMJ2ixokQ6c84dVHljOjfilAkuQhYMUg27QrHCep_UYAJ_LP8XoAHq4XWt6dKDj6TMslirnpnK5eHxi49Ac1U3frMNnQj92ba3FR4DnAGmAorteiZx2-ZsqdG_S3E)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
